 "proofs": {
  "claim": "total 2^129.279171 <= claim 129.39 - 0.10 and claim < 129.46",
  "detector": "bounded-memory detection: a 2-slot fingerprint ring compares fp(K) with fp(K-2) and one checkpoint register carries the running minimum fingerprint of the previous 64-step block; the escape doubles the minimum-fingerprint class, which depends only on the cycle, so merged walks stay merged. State is O(1) per trail (4 entries, 136 B each)",
  "doubled_add": "the transition canon(2X+T_j) is computed as X+(X+T_j): two batched affine additions, each 2M+1S+6A core plus one inverted denominator; 2 inversions per step at 3M of batch product work each",
  "meter": "escapes are arrivals priced inside S_ops, so the trial cost is step x S_ops + reports + setup = 2^129.279171; the headroom to 2^129.39 gives a Markov halt debit of 2^-65",
  "ord_2": "ord_r(2) = N is even, so 2^(N/2) = -1: the shortest sign-ambiguous gap is N/2 = 2^253.99999999966",
  "reports": "64-bit DP condition over 2^127.652966 steps gives 2^63.652966 reports <= 2^64 = cap/4; cap/mean per node is 5.087772; Chernoff puts cap loss below 2^-87651569754911473664",
  "routing": "the class key is the 256-bit x-coordinate; the DP predicate reads only bits 0..63 (through mix_low) and the router only bits 128..191 (through mix_high). The fields are disjoint, so a width-64 DP event pins one low-field value and leaves the routing field free: the route stays uniform over 2^16 and the v9b collapse cannot occur",
  "success": "model 1-0.60^1.21 = 0.4610; measured efficiency 0.90-0.95 gives 0.4267-0.4441; claim 0.39"
 },
